Player: This poster invites employees to meet for coffee and snacks. What should I do?

- Check whether the email address looks like a company address, then contact it
	Player: The address looks normal, so it should probably be safe.
	System: Safer, but lookalike addresses can be easy to miss, like google.com and gooogle.com.
	=> END

- Ask a coworker if they have heard about the event
	Player: If someone else knows about it, that should make it trustworthy.
	System: Not enough! Your coworker may have seen the same poster without verifying it either.
	=> END

- Verify the event through an official workplace source first
	Player: I'll check the company calendar or official directory before contacting anyone.
	System: Best choice! You verified the event independently instead of trusting the poster or email address.
	=> END